Description: fftools/ffmpeg_sched: unchoke every destination of a stream
 When the scheduler unchokes a demuxer, unchoke_for_stream() passed only
 the first element of each stream's destination array to
 unchoke_downstream(), and unchoke_downstream() did the same for each
 decoder output. A demuxed stream that is both stream-copied and decoded,
 or a decoder output that feeds two filter graphs, therefore never
 reached its later destinations.
 .
 A filter graph with sources of its own (have_sources) returns after
 every step and waits in sch_filter_receive() with best_input ==
 nb_inputs. Only a visit to one of its inputs unchokes it. When that
 input is a later destination, the graph waits forever while its full
 input queue blocks the decoder and the demuxer behind it, and FFmpeg
 deadlocks. Visit every destination instead.
Author: Streamarr
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-06
---
Index: FFmpeg/fftools/ffmpeg_sched.c
===================================================================
--- FFmpeg.orig/fftools/ffmpeg_sched.c
+++ FFmpeg/fftools/ffmpeg_sched.c
@@ -1295,7 +1295,8 @@ static void unchoke_downstream(Scheduler *sch, Schedul
     case SCH_NODE_TYPE_DEC:
         dec = &sch->dec[dst->idx];
         for (int i = 0; i < dec->nb_outputs; i++)
-            unchoke_downstream(sch, dec->outputs[i].dst);
+            for (int j = 0; j < dec->outputs[i].nb_dst; j++)
+                unchoke_downstream(sch, &dec->outputs[i].dst[j]);
         break;
     case SCH_NODE_TYPE_ENC:
         enc = &sch->enc[dst->idx];
@@ -1334,7 +1335,8 @@ static void unchoke_for_stream(Scheduler *sch, Schedul
                 return; // prevent infinite loop
             demux->waiter.choked_next = 0;
             for (int i = 0; i < demux->nb_streams; i++)
-                unchoke_downstream(sch, demux->streams[i].dst);
+                for (int j = 0; j < demux->streams[i].nb_dst; j++)
+                    unchoke_downstream(sch, &demux->streams[i].dst[j]);
             return;
         case SCH_NODE_TYPE_DEC:
             src = sch->dec[src.idx].src;
